 itecture of Ubiquity.Draft article (not for circulation).Michelle Nowlin
  Clinical Professor of Law and Co-Director of the Environmental Law and
  Policy Clinic at Duke University Law School. Presenting&#160\;Regulatory
  Challenges and Solutions to the Plastic Waste Pandemic.Moderator:Profess
 or Erica Lyman – Lewis &amp\; Clark Law School12:15-1:30pm | Lunch - Lu
 nch will be provided in the Student Lounge of the Legal Research Center o
 n campus1:30-3:00 | Panel 3 – U.S. Litigation OpportunitiesPanelists:Za
 k Smith– Senior Attorney and Director Global Biodiversity Conservation 
 at Natural Resources Defense Council (NRDC). Presenting Plastic Pollution
  and the Global Biodiversity Crisis: Can U.S. wildlife conservation laws 
 help deliver necessary transformative change?Sarah Morath– Professor of
  Law and Associate Dean for International Affairs at Wake Forest Universi
 ty of Law.Draft article (not for circulation).Presenting&#160\;The Landsc
 ape of U.S. Plastic Litigation: Litigation Pathways to Address a Global C
 risis.Dan Mensher '07 – Attorney at Keller Rohrback LLP. Presenting Pla
 stic Litigation for Plastic Problems: The Practical Opportunities and Cha
 llenges of Using Lawsuits to Address this Mess.Moderator:Professor Thomas
  Buchele – Lewis &amp\; Clark Law School3:00-3:15 Break3:15-4:45 | Pane
 l 4 – Hot TopicsPanelists:Hira Jaleel– Visiting Assistant Professor a
 t the Center for Animal Law Studies at Lewis &amp\; Clark Law School. Pre
 senting&#160\;Aquaculture's Plastic Problem.Amy Youngman '20 – Lawyer a
 nd Legal and Policy Specialist. Presenting Plastics in Fast Fashion - A R
 egulatory Gap.Juliette A. Jackson (https://www.linkedin.com/in/juliette-a
 -jackson-1a222678/) - Indigenous Rights Advocate and Executive Director o
 f Maqlaqs Gaa'tkni. Presenting&#160\;Stop Killing the Klamath: Rights of 
 Nature Solutions to Combat Pollution of Our Sacred Waters.Moderator:Profe
 ssor Daniel Rohlf – Lewis &amp\; Clark Law School4:45 pm | Reception fo
 r all attendees and speakers (Wood Hall Lounge)  Parking  Parking is limi
 ted at the law school\, and we highly encourage carpooling to our events.
  Due to its proximity to the law school\, we suggest parking in the Upper
  Griswold (https://www.lclark.edu/live/profiles/6366-parking-lot-c-upper-
 griswold) or Lower Griswold (https://www.lclark.edu/live/profiles/6367-pa
 rking-lot-d-lower-griswold) parking lot at the college campus (just a few
  minutes walk to the law school).&#160\;  For those unfamiliar with the c
 ampus\, you can access a full campus map here (https://www.lclark.edu/liv
 e/news/43826-updated-printable-campus-map).
