BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Literary Arts": "https://literary-arts.org/event/emergency-horse-magazine-launch/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:literary_arts
X-SOURCE:Literary Arts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260403T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260403T200000
DTSTAMP:20260402T192408
CREATED:20260310T215354Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260317T212840Z
UID:10005657-1775239200-1775246400@literary-arts.org
SUMMARY:Emergency Horse Launch
DESCRIPTION:The Literary Arts Bookstore & Cafe is pleased to welcome Emergency Horse for the launch of their latest issue. Join us for an evening of readings and celebration. \nThis event is free and open to all. \n\nAbout Emergency Horse \nThe relaunch of the magazine happened this past September. Emergency Horse #8 featured an interview of Robert Hunter\, an article about China’s complicity in the fentanyl scourge\, and another about an artist’s retreat being created on Ken Kesey’s farm. There was an examination of the importance of diversity in society\, and a story about Leprechauns in space. \nOriginally\, the publication existed in the early 1990s with distribution throughout the Northwest and northern California. Back in the day\, the contents featured the irreverent thoughts of the cartoonist Bill Callahan and Allen Ginsberg\, the writing of Charles Bukowski and Lew Welch\, and the advice of the ‘Old Insufferable Car Idiot.’ \nContact: emergencyhorse@gmail.com Attn: Darrin Daniel https://emergencyhorsemagazine.substack.com
URL:https://literary-arts.org/event/emergency-horse-magazine-launch/
LOCATION:Literary Arts
CATEGORIES:Free Events,Bookstore
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://literary-arts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Emergecy-Horse_600x900-scaled.jpg
GEO:45.5213897;-122.6810304
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Portland City Walking": "https://www.meetup.com/portland-city-walking-and-trail-walking-meetup-group/events/313809432/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_portland_city_walking
X-SOURCE:Meetup Portland City Walking
UID:event_313809432@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260325T021727Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260403T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260403T200000
SUMMARY:Bloom Hard 2: The Waitlist Strikes Back
DESCRIPTION:Portland City Trail Walking Group\nWe warned you. We told you this Magnolia Trail walk would be a full-scale sensory assault - an overwhelming\, relentless wall of color and bloom that could unhinge even the strongest among us. Thirty of you signed up anyway.\n\nNow dozens MORE of you have joined the waitlist\, apparently eager to get in line for the same floral devastation. At this point we have to ask: do you people not read warnings? Have you no sense of self-preservation?\n\nSo. We have decided to stop standing between you and your floral destruction and simply open a second session:\n\nThis is the evening edition. The golden hour edition. The you-waited-and-you-earned-it edition.\n\nWhat's coming for you: magnolias with an attitude. Waves of them. All blooming at once with zero regard for your emotional stability. And while you stand there trying to remember how to function\, we'll unpack how flowers actually reproduce - which is wilder than you think - and exactly how these magnolias were tracked down and convinced to move to Portland. Let’s just say these trees have some serious skeletons in their greenhouse.\n\nBring your device. This is a fully interactive presentation. We have gone deep on this. You will too.\n\nIt's a walk. It's a lecture. Honestly\, what else were you going to do on a Friday night?\n\nYou waited. You persisted. Journey on\, brave adventurer.\n\nThe Stats:\nMostly dirt trails with numerous benches\, vistas\, info placards.\nMeeting Point Location: Hoyt Arboretum Visitor Center\nMeeting Point Address: 4000 SW Fairview Blvd. Portland\, OR 97205\n[Google Maps](https://maps.app.goo.gl/Dro4F76PDhTSeJot6) Meeting Point\nMeeting Point GPS: 45.515833085577455\, -122.71565229736083\nMain Parking Area: [Hoyt Arboretum Paid Parking Lot 1](https://maps.app.goo.gl/aVrGfgmaBpviG5d98) & [Lot 2](https://maps.app.goo.gl/6ovXMX9qNUbutUu47)\nOverflow Parking Locations: [SW Fairview Blvd](https://maps.app.goo.gl/xKai57QowATiCUYRA)\, [Veteran’s Parking Lot](https://maps.app.goo.gl/6teqkktMY5TwJusA6) (8 min. walk)\, [Parking Lot B](https://maps.app.goo.gl/fwjKRPYfj5we8SM39) (12 min. walk).\n[Map of our hike](https://www.alltrails.com/explore/custom-routes/copy-pittock-to-hoyt-hoyt-start-9ee61b2?u=i&sh=xrhf7d). Press “preview route” to see animated trail.\nDistance: Approximately 1.2 miles\nElevation gain: 223 feet.\nEstimated time on trail: 1 hour hiking & 1 hour learning\nDifficulty level: Easy\nParking: Paid Parking Kitty Lots\nBathrooms at the trailhead at Hoyt Arboretum Visitor Center
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/portland-city-walking-and-trail-walking-meetup-group/events/313809432/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260317T041757Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260317T041757Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/5/5/2/a/600_533241802.jpeg
END:VEVENT
