DESCRIPTION:=======<br><br><b>Due to popular interest\, this event is <u>fu
 ll and closed</u></b>. Please consider signing-up for any of our other Apri
 l stewardship events!<br><br><br>=======<br>Your help is needed to mulch hu
 ndreds of plants that were planted this past winter at this natural area wi
 thin the Columbia Slough near Colwood Golf Center! We may also take out som
 e weedy introduced plants\, if time allows. <u>Note: there will be no tree-
 planting at this event\, and this can be physically-demanding work</u> (gre
 at for folks looking for a work out!).  Our stewardship events help to ensu
 re the highest level of plant survival through the PNW dry summer months ah
 ead.<p><i>**There is a 10-15 minute walk from the parking area to the plant
 ing site - look for our signs to guide you!**</i></p><p><b>Please arrive by
  9:45am</b> to find our tent and sign-in\, stewardship activities start pro
 mptly at 10:00am. We provide gloves\, tools\, and guidance. All you need to
  do is show up dressed for the weather and wearing sturdy shoes or boots (n
 o sandals of any kind\, please!) and be ready to have fun!</p><p><b>Under a
 ge 18?</b> We request that youth 15 and under volunteer with a parent/guard
 ian.  Youth 16 and older can volunteer on their own and will need to hand u
 s a <b><a href="https://friendsoftrees.org/youthwaiver" target="_blank"><u>
 <u><u><u><u><u>youth waiver form</u></u></u></u></u></u></a></b> signed by 
 their parent/guardian.</p><p><b>Questions?  </b>Pl<u></u>ease check out our
  <a href="https://friendsoftrees.org/volunteer-faq/" target="_blank"><u><u>
 <u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><b><u>Volunteer FAQ webpage</u></b></u></u></u><
 /u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a>.  Our team is also happy to assist! <a 
 href="mailto:Volunteer@friendsoftrees.org" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><
 u><u><u><u><u><u><b><u>volunteer@fr<u></u>iendsoftrees.or<u></u>g</u></b></
 u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a> / 503-595-0213 We look forwa
 rd to working together soon!<br></p><hr /><p>This event is in partnership w
 ith Portland Parks &amp\; Recreation and Portland OIC.</p>Funding for this 
 event is provided by the U.S. Department of Agriculture\, Forest Service.  
 This institution is an equal opportunity provider.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260331T191121Z
LOCATION:6373 NE Alderwood Rd\, Portland\, OR 97218\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
