SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260325T021732Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260406T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260406T193000
SUMMARY:Decompress + Connect Meditation Group
DESCRIPTION:Decompress + Connect Meditation Group\nDecompress and connect at the end of your work week with meditation practice and community. This event is in partnership with the Young Meditators Group of Portland.\n\nThis open session offers 20 minutes of silent meditation followed by a meditative talking circle practice\, and the opportunity to connect and socialize afterwards at a local pub.\n\n**No experience required\, and meditators of all traditions are welcome.**\n**Cushions will be provided but feel free to bring your own.**\n\n**SCHEDULE**\n\n**6:30 – 7:00PM Silent Meditation**\nSilent meditation practice (you are welcome to practice a silent meditation of your choosing)\n\n**7:00 – 7:25PM Meditative Talking Circle**\nResting on the foundation of meditation practice\, this talking circle practice expands to include others in the circle. While maintaining a meditation practice\, members of the circle are welcome to speak from the present moment\, though speaking is not required to participate. Instructions will be provided at the beginning so please arrive on time for this part of the practice.\n\n**7:25PM Closing and Social**\nThere will be some time after group to connect after practice\, after which the group may choose to go out for drinks and snacks at a nearby pub within walking distance.\n\nThis is a 'by donation' event. Suggested donation amount $3-10: [Please Donate Here](https://www.paypal.com/donate?hosted_button_id=PPCNJX8KYKY42)\n\nIf you are a regular member\, please consider signing up for a monthly donation- it helps make this group sustainable!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/decompress-connect/events/313779159/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260314T233359Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260314T233359Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/4/a/4/600_530905764.jpeg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lewis Clark": "https://www.lclark.edu/calendars/events/event/388930-keynote-lecture-with-dr-richard-wolff-scapegoats-sell"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lewis_clark
X-SOURCE:Lewis Clark
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260406T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260406T203000
SUMMARY:Keynote Lecture with Dr. Richard Wolff: Scapegoats & Sellouts: Na
 rratives of Capitalist Deception - International Affairs Symposium
DESCRIPTION:Moderated by: Elizabeth Bennett (https://college.lclark.edu/l
 ive/profiles/3380-elizabeth-bennett)  The widening gap of economic inequa
 lity between the capitalist and the worker leads to the rise in anti-fore
 ign and anti-immigrant rhetoric that paves the way for authoritarianism a
 nd fascist regimes. Progressive forces in Western nations have failed to 
 combat this authoritarian wave through properly representing working clas
 s interests\, instead letting tensions boil over. As unions are weakened\
 , austerity is implemented\, and the economy is privatized\, cultural res
 entment is used to channel frustrations of economic exploitation. Without
  a united working class\, authoritarianism is bound to succeed.  Dr. Rich
 ard Wolff is Professor of Economics Emeritus at the University of Massach
 usetts Amherst\, where he taught from 1973 to 2008\, and is currently a V
 isiting Professor in the Graduate Program in International Affairs at the
  New School University in New York City. He earned a BA in History from H
 arvard\, an MA in Economics from Stanford\, and both an MA and PhD in Eco
 nomics from Yale University. Named "America's most prominent Marxist econ
 omist" by The New York Times Magazine\, Dr. Wolff is widely recognized fo
 r his work on economic methodology\, class analysis\, and the structural 
 contradictions of capitalism. He is the co-founder of Democracy at Work\,
  a nonprofit that produces media and live events advocating workplace dem
 ocracy and critiquing capitalism\, and hosts the nationally syndicated pr
 ogram Economic Update.
