BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Reed College": "https://events.reed.edu/event/vocal-recital-haitham-haidar-tenor"}
X-SOURCE-ID:reed_college
X-SOURCE:Reed College
CATEGORIES:Performing Arts,Community
DESCRIPTION:Reed College Division of the Arts presents\n\nHaitham Haidar\, 
 tenor\n\nwith pianist Rebecca Stager\n\nfeaturing Reed College Chorus and C
 ollegium Musicum Fri Apr 10\, 20267:30pmReedwood Friends Church2901 SE Stee
 le St.Free and open to the public Join us Friday\, April 10 for a vocal rec
 ital and Q&A with Arts Divisional Guest Artist Haitham Haidar\, with pianis
 t Rebecca Stager and featuring Reed College's Chorus and Collegium Musicum.
  Haitham Haidar is a Lebanese-Palestinian Canadian tenor in demand internat
 ionally for his musicality\, “standout presence”\, and sensitive storytelli
 ng. He is a graduate of Yale’s Institute of Sacred Music\, McGill’s Schulic
 h School of Music\, and the University of British Columbia\, and currently 
 resides in Montreal\, Quebec. Haitham is praised for his ‘musical and lingu
 istic versatility’ and his ‘bright’ and ‘innately lyrical voice’ and enjoys
  performing oratorio\, opera\, and chamber music across North America\, Eur
 ope\, and Asia.\nHaitham's recent engagements as a tenor soloist include ap
 pearances with Early Music Vancouver\, Belgian ensemble Zefiro Torna (at th
 e Morgenland Festival in Osnabrück)\, Winnipeg Baroque Festival (Evangelist
  in Bach’s St. John Passion)\, TENET Vocal Artists in New York City\, Orche
 stre Arion in Montreal\, Folger Consort in Washington D.C. (Evangelist in S
 chütz’s Weinachtshistorie)\, Seraphic Fire in Miami\, and Skylark Ensemble 
 in Massachusetts.\nHaitham also has extensive experience as a recording art
 ist. His debut album Zaytoun explores the intersectionality of Baroque and 
 Arabic music\, and interlaces arias and devotional songs with poetry and mu
 sical improvisations. Haitham is featured as a vocal soloist on Austin-base
 d Conspirare’s Grammy-nominated album House of Belonging\, and his voice ca
 n be heard in one of the temples in Assassins Creed: Origins. Haitham also 
 records frequently as an ensemble vocalist and can be heard on Distance wit
 h the choir of St Andrew and St Paul in Montreal\, Schütz Christmas Story w
 ith Yale Schola Cantorum in New Haven\, L’Heure Mauve by Pierre LaPointe in
  Montreal.
DTEND:20260411T043000Z
DTSTAMP:20260403T022346Z
DTSTART:20260411T023000Z
GEO:45.485215;-122.635717
LOCATION:Reedwood Friends Church
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Vocal Recital: Haitham Haidar\, tenor
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52314006434399
URL:https://events.reed.edu/event/vocal-recital-haitham-haidar-tenor
END:VEVENT
