 arkdown-new-styling"><p data-start="80" data-end="623"><strong><a href="h
 ttps://www.lclark.edu/live/profiles/14032-shawn-filippi-99">Shawn Filippi
 </a></strong> JD'99 has spent over 25 years advising boards of directors\
 , CEOs\, and executive teams through complex legal\, regulatory\, governa
 nce\, compliance\, and business issues. She currently serves as Head of P
 olicy Engagement and Advocacy at the National Society for Corporate Gover
 nance\, where she also chairs the national Small- and Mid-Cap Public Comp
 any Committee. In those roles she engages in advocacy work with the SEC a
 nd legislative\, regulatory\, judicial\, and other policy-making and stan
 dard-setting entities on behalf of public and complex private companies n
 ationally.                </p><p data-start="80" data-end="623">         
          Previously\, Shawn spent over a decade as Vice President\, Chief
  Compliance Officer\, and Corporate Secretary of NW Natural Holdings and 
 NW Natural\, and prior to that\, held a variety of legal leadership posit
 ions supporting all aspects of those same businesses. Before that\, she w
 as an attorney at Stoel Rives LLP\, focusing her practice on corporate\, 
 securities and finance\, and mergers and acquisitions. She started her ca
 reer clerking in the Special Litigation Unit of Oregon Department of Just
 ice.                </p><p>                  Despite the demands of her c
 areer\, Shawn found time to give back and support Lewis &amp\; Clark Law 
 School. She currently serves on two leadership boards for the school: the
  Board of Visitors and the Center for Business Law and Leadership. Relati
 vely shortly after her graduation in 1999\, she led the Alumni Board as p
 resident from 2001 - 2006. In addition to her work at Lewis &amp\; Clark 
 boards\, she currently serves as a board member of the KARES Foundation\,
  a national nonprofit focused on an ultra-rare neurodevelopmental genetic
  condition\, and is a board member of the Pacific Northwest Chapter of th
 e Society for Corporate Governance and serves on the Advisory Counsel for
  the PDX Corporate Counsel Forums.                </p></div></div></div><
 /div></div></div></article></div>
