BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Reed College": "https://events.reed.edu/event/seeds-for-liberation-film-screening-and-director-qa"}
X-SOURCE-ID:reed_college
X-SOURCE:Reed College
CATEGORIES:Exhibition,Community
DESCRIPTION:All are welcome to our special Portland screening of "Seeds for
  Liberation" on Wednesday April 15\, at 5:30pm at Reed College's Psychology
  Building\, Room 105. Joining us this evening are Abby Martin and Dr. Mimi 
 Syed\, who are featured in the film\, along with Director Matthew Solomon a
 nd Executive Producer Donna Hadjikhani.\n\nLocation: Reed College\, Psychol
 ogy Building\, Room 105\n\nCampus map hereGoogle Maps link here \n\nAbout "
 Seeds for Liberation"\n\n"Seeds for Liberation" explores Palestinian resist
 ance through emotional and impactful interviews with historians\, activists
 \, and experts. The film shows how social media has exposed daily life in G
 aza and the West Bank\, challenging dominant Western narratives\, and it hi
 ghlights a transnational\, anti-imperialist struggle rooted in solidarity a
 nd collective justice.\n\nIn this new documentary from Director Matthew Sol
 omon and Executive Producer Donna Hadjikhani of “Reimagining Safety\,” join
 ed by Executive Producer Alana Hadid\, experts discuss the impact of Palest
 ine’s 77-year occupation by Israeli forces\, the role social media has play
 ed in mobilizing global support\, and provide a roadmap for collective libe
 ration. The film includes impactful and emotional interviews with legal sch
 olars\, activists\, and members of The Black Liberation Army\, La Raza Unid
 a\, and the Stop Cop City movement who illustrate the effects of Israeli an
 d U.S. imperialism and colonialism\, what “Free Palestine” means\, and how 
 it can be achieved.
DTEND:20260416T033000Z
DTSTAMP:20260403T022346Z
DTSTART:20260416T003000Z
GEO:45.480644;-122.627381
LOCATION:Psychology\, 105
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Seeds for Liberation: Film Screening and Director Q&A
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52313825231110
URL:https://events.reed.edu/event/seeds-for-liberation-film-screening-and-d
 irector-qa
END:VEVENT
