  the upcoming 26/27 academic year? A student job gives you real world exp
 erience that is flexible with your class schedule. Find out more informat
 ion at the Job Fair featured at our upcoming Spring Week of Welcome event
  happening the first week of Spring Term 2026.There will also be the Pass
 ports to Success activity. Complete your passport by collecting stamps an
 d earn a $15 voucher redeemable at any PCC Cafeteria.Spring Week of Welco
 me Student Job Fair &amp\; Passports to Success is happening from 10am–
 2pm daily at the following locations:Monday\, April 13: Rock Creek Bldg 5
  Room 122Tuesday\, April 14: Sylvania CC Main MallWednesday\, April 15: S
 outheast MTH Great HallThursday\, April 16: Cascade 2nd Floor Lobby &amp\
 ; Rooms 202\, 203\, 204The division of Student Wellbeing\, Engagement and
  Belonging (SWEB) is hiring including:Associated Students of Portland Com
 munity CollegeCivic Leadership DevelopmentMulticultural CenterQueer Resou
 rce CenterStudent Basic Needs CenterStudent EngagementVeterans Resource C
 enterWomen's Resource CenterThis event is a Drive2Thrive point-earning ac
 tivity.Learn more about Drive2Thrive at pcc.edu/d2t*This event is FREE an
 d in-person only. Only PCC students currently taking classes may particip
 ate. Supplies are limited and will be offered on a first-come\, first-ser
 ved basis at the time of the event. We cannot ship items to students and/
 or set items aside to be picked up later.Spring Week of Welcome Job Fair 
 with Passports to Success is brought to you by Student Engagement. The of
 fice of Student Engagement is pleased to offer accommodations to ensure t
 hat our programs are accessible and inclusive. Please email a request\, q
 uestions\, and thoughts to: pcc_engage-group@pcc.edu as soon as possible.
 —Event Details: https://hub.pcc.edu/rsvp?id=382359 (https://hub.pcc.edu
 /rsvp?id=382359)
