DTEND:20260418T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260403T022438Z
UID:5g89il6vm7o4he2tbdb6igqced@google.com
CREATED:20260123T231648Z
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Earth Week by mulching hundreds of native plants that
  were planted this past winter at Nadaka Nature Park! We may also take out 
 some weedy introduced plants\, if time allows. <br><u><br></u><br><u>Fun de
 tail</u>: we are also hosting a plant giveaway at this event\, and will hav
 e native trees\, shrubs\, and wildflowers to give away to volunteers and me
 mbers of the public.<br><br><u>There will be no tree-planting at this event
 \, and this can be physically-demanding work</u> (great for folks looking f
 or a work out!).  Our stewardship events help to ensure the highest level o
 f plant survival through the PNW dry summer months ahead.<p><b>How do I reg
 ister? </b>Register by filling out <b><a href="https://www.tfaforms.com/484
 0511?tfa_26=a0TPa00001Edi8k&tfa_2189=Nadaka%20Nature%20Park%20Stewardship\,
 %20Gresham&tfa_31=a0VPa00000DfdED&tfa_45=%20at%20April%2018\,%202026%20at%2
 09:45%20am&tfa_2190=2026-04-18&tfa_49=3.25&tfa_886=Standard%20FOT&tfa_51=of
 fsite" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u>this quick form</u></u></u></u></a></b>.
   Groups\, families\, and individuals welcome!</p><u></u><p><b>Please arriv
 e by 9:45am</b> to find our tent and sign-in\, stewardship activities start
  promptly at 10:00am. We provide gloves\, tools\, and guidance. All you nee
 d to do is show up dressed for the weather and wearing sturdy shoes or boot
 s (no sandals of any kind\, please!) and be ready to have fun!</p><p><b>Und
 er age 18?</b> We request that youth 15 and under volunteer with a parent/g
 uardian.  Youth 16 and older can volunteer on their own and will need to ha
 nd us a <b><a href="https://friendsoftrees.org/youthwaiver" target="_blank"
 ><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>youth waiver form</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></
 u></u></a></b> signed by their parent/guardian.</p><p><b>Questions?  </b>Pl
 <u></u>ease check out our <a href="https://friendsoftrees.org/volunteer-faq
 /" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><b><u>Volunteer FAQ web
 page</u></b></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a>.  Our team is 
 also happy to assist! <a href="mailto:Volunteer@friendsoftrees.org" target=
 "_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><b><u>volunteer@fr<u></u>iendsoft
 rees.or<u></u>g</u></b></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a> / 5
 03-595-0213 We look forward to working together soon!</p><hr /><p>This even
 t is in partnership with City of Gresham and Portland OIC.</p>Funding for t
 his event is provided by the U.S. Department of Agriculture\, Forest Servic
 e.  This institution is an equal opportunity provider.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260330T213131Z
