SUMMARY:Homework Help
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T003000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T010000Z
UID:69b844ea8d5e2d093365a132@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Homework Help each Tuesday 5:30-6:00 and 6:00- 6:30 p.m. in 
 the library.\nWe’re happy to offer free homework help! Homework Help is 
 offered for all subjects\, specializing in English\, French\, Math\, and S
 cience for all grade levels\, K through College Level. Tutoring with Jenna
  W.\, PhD is offered for all subjects\, Sessions are a half hour each. Reg
 ister online\, no library card is needed to register.\nIf accommodations w
 ould help you attend one of our library classes or events\, please ask. Ou
 r library events are always free!
LOCATION:North Plains Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b844ea8d5e2d093365a132
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wccls Library": "https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f9fb58b29ea2800d28bcc"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wccls_library
SUMMARY:Makerspace Open Lab
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T003000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T023000Z
UID:699f9fb58b29ea2800d28bcc@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Makerspace Open Labs are for anyone who wants to check out the
  space and use our equipment to make cool things. Room assistants are avai
 lable to guide you in the basic use of the tools and technology. Come in w
 ith an idea and leave with a finished project! For more information about 
 the Makerspace and its resources\,\nsee here\n.\nMakerspace Open Labs take
  place on the following weekly schedule:\nTuesdays\n\, 5:30 - 7:30PM\nThur
 sdays\n\, 4:00 - 6:00PM\nSaturdays\n\, 10:00 AM - 1:00PM\nSundays\n\, 1:30
  - 5:30P\nEach month we provide the materials\, tools and instructions for
  a featured Makerspace project that everyone is invited to try.\nApril's f
 eatured project is Seed Paper bookmarks (pictured).\nIMPORTANT:\nAdults us
 ing the Makerspace for the first time need to\nsign a waiver\n\; people un
 der the age of 18 must have a waiver signed by a parent or guardian.\nYou 
 can sign and submit waivers online here.
LOCATION:Tualatin Public Library\, Makerspace
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f9fb58b29ea2800d28bcc
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
