BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lan Su Garden": "https://lansugarden.org/event/steep-paint-magnolia-april-24/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lan_su_garden
X-SOURCE:Lan Su Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T170000
DTSTAMP:20260402T192428
CREATED:20260313T051651Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260401T193514Z
UID:10000880-1777039200-1777050000@lansugarden.org
SUMMARY:Steep & Paint: Magnolia with Dorota Haber-Lehigh
DESCRIPTION:Instructor | Tickets | Series Schedule | Parking \n\n\n\nEnjoy a blossom-filled afternoon at the beautiful Lan Su Chinese Garden with the return of Steep & Paint. With all materials provided and admission included\, all you need to bring is yourself! \n\n\n\nWe’re bringing this series back by popular demand and newly reimagined in partnership with the Oregon Botanical Artists (OBA). This immersive afternoon experience invites you to slow down\, look closely\, and connect with plants through tea\, conversation\, and hands-on art-making. Our August 14 Lotus session with Zebith Thalden will use colored pencils as the medium. \n\n\n\nEach session weaves together horticulture\, tea culture\, and botanical art in a relaxed\, welcoming setting: \n\n\n\n\nLearn the plant up close: A Lan Su gardener leads a close-up botanical show-and-tell\, sharing seasonal plant facts\, cultural stories\, and growing insights.\n\n\n\nTaste the season: Enjoy a sampling of seasonal teas from Yun Shui Teahouse.\n\n\n\nCreate botanical art: An OBA artist guides a full botanical art class inspired by the featured plant.\n\n\n\n\nWhether you’re returning to Steep & Paint or joining for the first time\, this refreshed program offers an even richer way to experience Lan Su. Bring a friend with you and let’s Steep & Paint together! \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMeet the Instructor: Dorota Haber-Lehigh \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n“Nootka Rose and Ana’s Hummingbird” by Dorota Haber-Lehigh \n\n\n\n\n\nDorota Haber-Lehigh is a botanical artist and educator whose work explores the connections between ecology\, healing\, medicinal plants\, and human relationships with the natural world. She holds a Diploma in Botanical Illustration from the Society of Botanical Artists in the UK\, along with degrees in Art\, International Studies\, and teaching. Originally from Poland\, Dorota’s work is shaped by themes of resilience\, memory\, and healing in nature. She has created and contributed to several botanical and ethnobotanical coloring books\, and her work has been exhibited regionally and nationally\, including at Portland Japanese Garden\, Lan Su Chinese Garden\, and juried exhibitions focused on native plants and ecological art. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMeet Our Partner: Oregon Botanical Artists (OBA)  \n\n\n\nOregon Botanical Artists is a nonprofit organization dedicated to promoting contemporary botanical art while honoring its long-standing traditions. Founded in 2012\, the organization supports a diverse community of artists who celebrate the beauty and diversity of plant life through detailed and scientifically informed artwork. Oregon Botanical Artists is affiliated with the American Society of Botanical Artists as an Artists Circle. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nInstructor | Tickets | Series Schedule | Parking \n\n\n\nSteep & Paint Need to Know \n\n\n\nEach class session is independent — participants are welcome to register for any individual class without attending others. \n\n\n\nRegistration fee includes full-day admission to Lan Su Chinese Garden. \n\n\n\nGet Tickets\n\n\n\n\nLan Su Members & Guests: $56.95\n\n\n\nGeneral: $66.95\n\n\n\n\nNote: A $0.95 service fee is reflected in each paid ticket \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFull Series Schedule\n\n\n\nSet a new monthly Friday tradition\, or treat someone special to an amazing afternoon of creativity!  \n\n\n\n\n                \n                \n                            \n                            \n                            \n                    \n            \n    \n    \n    \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nParking & Directions\n\n\n\nFree Lan Su Parking\n\n\n\nThere is free first come\, first served parking in our sister lot next to the garden at 424 NW Third Avenue. Additional metered parking and garages are available on surrounding streets.
URL:https://lansugarden.org/event/steep-paint-magnolia-april-24/
LOCATION:Lan Su Chinese Garden\, 239 NW Everett Street\, Portland\, Oregon\, 97209
CATEGORIES:Art,Magnolia Festival,Tea
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://lansugarden.org/wp-content/uploads/steep-and-paint-2026.webp
END:VEVENT
