X-SOURCE:Friends Of Trees Green Space
DTSTART:20260425T164500Z
DTEND:20260425T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260403T022438Z
UID:3lnsv1bheagsc4i8hrk3lnp4h8@google.com
CREATED:20260123T232520Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><strong><b>Celebrate Earth Week with the </b></strong><a hre
 f="https://friendsoftrees.org/blog/greening-wilkes/" target="_blank"><u><st
 rong><b>Greening Wilkes</b></strong></u></a><strong><b> collective by mulch
 ing hundreds of native pollinator-friendly species at Wilkes Creek Headwate
 rs! </b></strong>We may also take out some weedy introduced plants\, if tim
 e allows. <u>Note</u>: there will be no tree-planting at this event\, and t
 his can be physically-demanding work (great for folks looking for a work ou
 t!). Our stewardship events help to ensure the highest level of plant survi
 val through the PNW dry summer months ahead. <b>This event will include bir
 d walks led by the Bird Alliance of Oregon\, and will end by 12pm so that p
 eople can join the Greening Wilkes celebration from 12-1:30 at nearby Wilke
 s Park. </b></p><p>The celebration will involve lunch\, tabling and games f
 rom the Greening Wilkes partners- Portland Parks and Recreation\, Columbia 
 Slough Watershed Council\, Verde\, and The Bird Alliance of Oregon- as well
  as a native plant giveaway hosted by Friends of Trees! (Registration is no
 t required to join the celebration\, but it is to participate in the stewar
 dship event.) </p><p><b>How do I register? </b>Register by filling out <b><
 a href="https://www.tfaforms.com/4840511?tfa_26=a0TPa00001Edi8m&tfa_2189=Wi
 lkes%20Creek%20Headwaters%20Stewardship\,%20NE%20Portland&tfa_31=a0VPa00000
 DfdEJ&tfa_45=%20at%20April%2025\,%202026%20at%209:45%20am&tfa_2190=2026-04-
 25&tfa_49=3.25&tfa_886=Portland%20Parks%20and%20Recreation&tfa_51=offsite" 
 target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u>this quick form</u></u></u></u></u></u></
 a></b>.  Groups\, families\, and individuals welcome!</p><u></u><p><b>Pleas
 e arrive by 9:45am</b> to find our tent and sign-in\, stewardship activitie
 s start promptly at 10:00am. We provide gloves\, tools\, and guidance. All 
 you need to do is show up dressed for the weather and wearing sturdy shoes 
 or boots (no sandals of any kind\, please!) and be ready to have fun!</p><p
 ><b>Under age 18?</b> We request that youth 15 and under volunteer with a p
 arent/guardian.  Youth 16 and older can volunteer on their own and will nee
 d to hand us a <b><a href="https://friendsoftrees.org/youthwaiver" target="
 _blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>youth waiver form</u></u></u></u><
 /u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a></b> signed by their parent/guardian.</p><p>
 <b>Questions?  </b>Pl<u></u>ease check out our <a href="https://friendsoftr
 ees.org/volunteer-faq/" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u
 ><u><b><u>Volunteer FAQ webpage</u></b></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u>
 </u></u></u></u></a>.  Our team is also happy to assist! <a href="mailto:Vo
 lunteer@friendsoftrees.org" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><
 u><u><u><b><u>volunteer@fr<u></u>iendsoftrees.or<u></u>g</u></b></u></u></u
 ></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a> / 503-595-0213 We look forwar
 d to working together soon!</p><hr /><p>This event is in partnership with P
 ortland Parks &amp\; Recreation and Portland OIC.</p><p>Funding for this ev
 ent is provided by the U.S. Department of Agriculture\, Forest Service.  Th
 is institution is an equal opportunity provider.</p>
