SUMMARY:Crystal Ballroom History & Art Tour
DESCRIPTION:Tour will meet outside the Box Office  \nJoin us as we explore the rich history of the Crystal Ballroom\, including police raids\, visits by silent screen idols and Beat poets\, psychedelic light shows\, R&B and rock legends\, dancing throughout the decades and narrow escapes from ruin.  \nThis tour may require standing for long periods of time and is mostly accessible via elevator. One stop on the tour\, the balcony\, can be seen but not accessed\, except by stairs.  \nPassport holders: This tour is eligible for the Crystal Ballroom and Lola’s Room location stamps and the Attend a History Sponsored Event experience stamp.
URL:https://www.crystalballroompdx.com/events/275938-crystal-ballroom-history-art-tour/
CATEGORIES:April
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.crystalballroompdx.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/CrystalBallroomTours25-ACh39k.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Literary Arts": "https://literary-arts.org/event/the-sijo-crash-course-in-traditional-korean-poetry/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:literary_arts
X-SOURCE:Literary Arts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T120000
DTSTAMP:20260402T192408
CREATED:20260122T232208Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260320T233204Z
UID:10005624-1777197600-1777204800@literary-arts.org
SUMMARY:The Sijo: Poetry Workshop in Korean Traditional Form
DESCRIPTION:The sijo is Korea’s most prominent and enduring traditional poetic form. Characterized by a clarity and accessibility that belies emotional complexity and tonal nuance\, it is a form that prioritizes the unsaid and best grapples with the unsayable. Its brevity demands strict economy of language and intentionality of silence. Writing in this discipline exercises several poetic skills that we will focus on and hone throughout this six-week workshop.\nReadings will engage with both traditional and contemporary examples of sijo poetry\, as well as some poems from jisei\, tanka\, haiku\, and jueju traditions. All readings will be in English or translated into English. No Korean language skills are required.\nThis workshop invites poets of all levels to write outside their comfort zone. All students will have the opportunity to have at least two poems workshopped by the course with detailed instructor feedback.\nStudents should bring a notebook and writing utensil\, and are expected to bring their annotated copies of the poems being workshopped on a given day\, as well as course readings. \nAccess Program\nWe want our writing classes and seminars to be accessible to everyone\, regardless of income and background. We understand that our tuition structure can present obstacles for some people. Our Access Program offers writing class and seminar tuitions at a reduced rate. Most writing classes have at least one access spot available. \nPlease apply here for access rate tuition. Contact Susan Moore at susan@literary-arts.org if you have questions. \nLiaison position\nEvery in-person class and seminar at Literary Arts has one liaison position. Liaisons perform specific duties for each class meeting. If you are a liaison for a class or seminar\, the full amount of your tuition is covered by Literary Arts. Apply here for the liaison position.
URL:https://literary-arts.org/event/the-sijo-crash-course-in-traditional-korean-poetry/
LOCATION:Literary Arts
CATEGORIES:Writing Classes,In-person
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://literary-arts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Classes26_WebGraphics_600x900_Fillable-1-1.png
GEO:45.5213897;-122.6810304
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Literary Arts": "https://literary-arts.org/event/bring-your-story-to-the-stage/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:literary_arts
X-SOURCE:Literary Arts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T143000
DTSTAMP:20260402T192408
CREATED:20260202T210700Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260227T200339Z
UID:10005631-1777197600-1777213800@literary-arts.org
SUMMARY:Bring Your Story to the Stage
DESCRIPTION:This class is for anyone ready to take a personal 5-minute story and actively shape it for an audience. You’ll work hands-on with one story. Drafting\, refining\, and testing it aloud. We’ll focus on structure\, pacing\, and point of view\, helping you find the spine of the story and decide what belongs in this particular version of the story and what doesn’t. You’ll practice starting strong\, building momentum\, and landing the story with intention. \nTaught by BACKFENCE Storytelling producers and hosts Frayn Masters and Ash Allen\, this class is ideal if you’ve taken Small Stories\, Big Meaning or already have a personal story you’re curious to bring forward—whether for a stage\, or simply to hear it land out loud. \nRather than “performing\,” this class emphasizes shaping a vulnerable narrative. You’ll receive demonstrations and feedback on mic use\, voice\, presence\, and timing in a supportive room\, with clear guidance.  \nBy the end of the workshop\, you’ll have:\n•	A shaped draft you can continue developing\n•	Practical tools for revising and rehearsing\n•	Greater confidence telling a personal story aloud\n•	A clearer sense of how you want to show up onstage \nYou set the pace. Participation is encouraged but never forced. The goal is clarity\, connection\, and momentum—not polish or performance. \nstrong>Access Program\nWe want our classes and seminars to be accessible to everyone\, regardless of income and background. We understand that our tuition structure can present obstacles for some people. Our Access Program offers writing class and seminar tuitions at a reduced rate. Most classes have at least one access spot available. \nPlease apply here for access rate tuition. Contact Susan Moore at susan@literary-arts.org if you have questions. \nLiaison position\nEvery in-person class and seminar at Literary Arts has one liaison position. Liaisons perform specific duties for each class meeting. If you are a liaison for a class or seminar\, the full amount of your tuition is covered by Literary Arts. \nApply here for the liaison position.
URL:https://literary-arts.org/event/bring-your-story-to-the-stage/
CATEGORIES:Writing Classes,In-person,Storytelling
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://literary-arts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/template.jpeg
END:VEVENT
