DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260429T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260429T203000
DTSTAMP:20260402T192408
CREATED:20260312T181437Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260317T232005Z
UID:10005665-1777489200-1777494600@literary-arts.org
SUMMARY:BIPOC Reading Series - April
DESCRIPTION:This monthly reading series is intended to prioritize the safety\, creativity\, and stories of Black people\, Indigenous people\, and People of Color. \nCome listen to our featured readers\, or sign up to share your work in our open mic. Readings will be followed by a short community discussion. Hosted by Kyle Yoshioka and Jessica Meza-Torres. The featured reader for April is Paul Susi. \nThis event is open to everyone\, but only people who identify as Black\, Indigenous\, and/or People of Color will be invited to read. If you have any questions\, please contact Jessica Meza-Torres at jmezatorres24@gmail.com or Kyle Yoshioka at kyle.yoshioka@gmail.com.
URL:https://literary-arts.org/event/bipoc-reading-series-april-2/
LOCATION:Literary Arts
CATEGORIES:Free Events,In-person
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://literary-arts.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/BookstoreEvents_Evergreen-Templates_600x900_BIPOCRS.jpg
GEO:45.5213897;-122.6810304
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Portland Fun Run": "https://www.meetup.com/portland-fun-run/events/jtsmwtyjcgbmc/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_portland_fun_run
X-SOURCE:Meetup Portland Fun Run
UID:event_jtsmwtyjcgbmc@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260325T021729Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260429T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260429T220000
SUMMARY:Run & Chug!
DESCRIPTION:Portland Fun Run\nThe route will be posted soon! In the meantime\, here are some FAQs:\n\n**Where do I find the group?**\nWe typically meet up right outside the bar! We rotate through a variety of bars and breweries. Check out our past events to see what places we typically go to.\n\n**What is the average pace of the group?**\nThere is a wide range of paces that varies week-to-week\, but typically most people are between 7:30 - 10 minute miles. We welcome all runners\, regardless of pace (the #1 goal our group is to make new friends\, not break records)\, but we advise making sure you are comfortable with the route if you are worried you might be slower than this range\, just so you don’t get lost.\n\n* Need a running buddy or want to check if anyone else in the group is running your pace? Feel free to message Erin to coordinate this! Please send any messages by Tuesday evening the day before we meet 😊\n\n**What time does the group actually start running?**\nWe suggest runners arrive around 6:55pm\, but we do not actually start running until 7:05pm.\n\n**When is the route posted?**\nThe route is posted typically Tuesday night or Wednesday morning.\nI don’t have a car\, what do I do with my belongings while I’m running?\nOne option is to wear a running belt to keep keys\, ID\, credit card\, etc. on you while you run\, but if you show up a little early\, you can often find someone who is willing to put your jacket or other belongings in their car for you during the run.\n\n**What should I bring?**\nMake sure to bring your ID and credit card/cash for the bar. Additionally\, in the winter\, we recommend bringing a light to run with and wearing something reflective. Lastly\, we are sometimes outside for drinks\, depending on the location\, so it’s a good idea to bring a jacket.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/portland-fun-run/events/jtsmwtyjcgbmc/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260316T195718Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260316T195718Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/5/a/6/1/600_503363137.jpeg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ohsu Library": "https://librarycalendar.ohsu.edu/event/16531743"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ohsu_library
X-SOURCE:Ohsu Library
DTSTART:20260429T190000Z
DTEND:20260429T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260429T000000Z
SUMMARY:Truth or Fiction? Verifying AI-Generated Answers
DESCRIPTION:Generative artificial intelligence tools like ChatGPT can 
 produce convincing answers\, but not all of them are based on reliable 
 sources. In this hands-on workshop\, you’ll learn how to write balanced 
 prompts to reduce bias in text generated by common AI chatbots such as 
 ChatGPT\, and how to fact-check those responses using proven information 
 literacy strategies. This session will demonstrate practical skills to use 
 AI chatbots responsibly and verify the accuracy of the text they 
 generate.\n\nAfter the session\, learners will be able to:\n\n\n	Craft 
 effective prompts for use with public generative AI chatbots such as 
 ChatGPT\, Gemini\, Claude\, etc.\n	Describe the strengths and limitations 
 of generative AI for information search and retrieval\n	Use information 
 literacy skills and tools to evaluate AI-generated text output\n\n\nThis 
 workshop will be recorded\, and the recording will be shared with all 
 registered attendees after the session. If you cannot make the workshop 
 date and time\, you are welcome to register in order to receive a copy of 
 the recording.
LOCATION:Virtual
ORGANIZER;CN="Kristin Whitman":MAILTO:whitmank@ohsu.edu
CATEGORIES:AI
UID:LibCal-6248-16531743
URL:https://librarycalendar.ohsu.edu/event/16531743
END:VEVENT
