X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Tockify Theoldchurch": "https://events.tocportland.org/theoldchurch/detail/784/1777489200000"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tockify_theoldchurch
X-SOURCE:Tockify Theoldchurch
UID:TKF/6255f70a970e2a7c613b11d0/784/29624820/0/0
DTSTART:20260429T190000Z
DTEND:20260429T200000Z
URL:https://events.tocportland.org/theoldchurch/detail/784/1777489200000
SUMMARY: Mid-day Break Concert with David Rothman
DESCRIPTION:Concert pianist David Rothman performs 8 Noveletten\, Opus 21
  and Piano Concerto in A major by Robert Schumann\, with Michael Barnes\,
  organ as orchestra.\n\nPianist David Rothman has delighted TOC audiences
  with performances of the entire Schubert Cycle\, Mozart Cycle\, and all 
 of Chopin’s solo piano pieces. With Michael Barnes on the organ\, Rothman
  has also played the Rachmaninoff Third and Brahms Second Piano Concerto 
 at TOC. As a child\, Rothman attended the Yehudi Menuhin School\, then th
 e Curtis Institute of Music.\n\nMichael Barnes is a professional pianist 
 and organist\, and has been Senior Organist at Westminster since 1992. Wi
 th the Westminster Presbyterian Church Chancel Choir\, he has toured Scot
 land and Cuba. He has performed with the Wednesday Noon Concert Series at
  The Old Church Concert Hall since 1988. With the Portland Gay Men's Chor
 us\, he toured China for goodwill concerts in 2019. He accompanies the Pa
 cific Youth Choir\, and is Organist at Westminster Presbyterian Church an
 d Temple Beth Israel in Portland\, OR. He is a member of the American Gui
 ld of Organists\, Organ Historical Society and Guild of Temple Musicians.
 \n\nWATCH THE LIVESTREAM https://youtube.com/live/ooVn8zfxnM4\n\nProgram\
 n\nRobert Schumann\n8 Noveletten\, Opus 21\n\n1. No 1 in F major\n\n2. No
 . 2 in D major\n\n3. No. 3 in D major\n\n4. No. 4 in D major\n\n5. No. 5 
 in D major\n6. No. 6 in A major\n7. No. 7 in E major\n\n9. No. 8 in F# mi
 nor\n\nIntermission\n\nRobert Schumann\nConcerto in A minor\n\n1. Allegro
  affettuoso (A minor)\n\n2. Intermezzo: Andantino grazioso (F major)\n\n3
 . Allegro vivace (A major)
CATEGORIES:lunchtime-concerts
