BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Japanese Garden": "https://japanesegarden.org/events/sogetsu-portland-rose-show/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:japanese_garden
X-SOURCE:Japanese Garden
UID:5315@japanesegarden.org
DTSTART:20260523T170000Z
DTEND:20260525T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260402T160936Z
URL:https://japanesegarden.org/events/sogetsu-portland-rose-show/
SUMMARY:Sogetsu Portland Rose Show
DESCRIPTION:\nAn arrangement from Sogetsu Portland Branch’s Virtual Rose Show in 2020\, made by Don Davidson\n\n\n\nSaturday\,&nbsp\;May 23rd\, 2026&nbsp\;/&nbsp\;10:00am –&nbsp\;5:00pm&nbsp\;\n\n\n\nSunday\,&nbsp\;May 24th\, 2026&nbsp\;/ 10:00am – 4:30 pm&nbsp\;\n\n\n\n*This show will also be open during Member Hours starting at 9:00am.  \n\n\n\nSee stunning works created by local ikebana artists featuring&nbsp\;Portland‘s favorite flower as the city celebrates its beloved tradition\, the Rose Festival.&nbsp\;\n\n\n\nThe Sogetsu School of Ikebana believes ikebana can be practiced anytime\, anywhere\, by anyone. Local artists from the Sogetsu Portland Branch will create a wide range of styles from basic to abstract which use objects of sculptural intent and character. The three main elements designers use are line\, mass\, and color\, with an emphasis on the designer’s individual artistic expression and creativity. Visit the Garden to see how their arrangements both suit and enhance the Yanai Classroom in the Jordan Schnitzer Japanese Arts Learning Center.&nbsp\;\n\n\n\nIkebana\, a Japanese artform\, has been translated as “living flowers” or “giving life to flowers\,” and is unique from other approaches to flower arrangement. In ikebana\, asymmetry and the use of empty space are essential features of the overall composition. A sense of harmony among the materials\, the container\, and the setting is also crucial.&nbsp\;\n\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://wpmedia.japanesegarden.org/w:2203/h:1729/q:mauto/process:50426/id:8e234095e942e316d85895361d9ebc47/https://japanesegarden.org/Don2.jpg
CATEGORIES:Botanical Exhibitions
