BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Japanese Garden": "https://japanesegarden.org/events/textile-workshop-portland-japanese-garden-inspired-stitched-vignette/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:japanese_garden
X-SOURCE:Japanese Garden
UID:5185@japanesegarden.org
DTSTART:20260603T163000Z
DTEND:20260603T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260221T054845Z
URL:https://japanesegarden.org/events/textile-workshop-portland-japanese-garden-inspired-stitched-vignette/
SUMMARY:Textile Workshop: Portland Japanese Garden-Inspired Stitched Vignette with Judilee Fitzhugh
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\n\n\nPortland Japanese Garden is partnering with textile artisan Judilee Fitzhugh to offer a series of four immersive textile workshops. In each session\, participants will relax and enjoy the rhythmic dance of needle and thread while learning the meditative art of hand-stitching to create Japanese- and garden-inspired projects.\n\n\n\nThis workshop runs from 9:30am–4:00pm\, including six hours of instruction and a 30-minute lunch break. Participation is limited to 20 students per workshop\, and classes are open to students of all levels of sewing experience.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWorkshop Description\n\n\n\nYou will begin this workshop by spending some time in the&nbsp\;Garden&nbsp\;to take photos or sketches of a scene or object that resonates with you (there will also be printed photographs available to use for inspiration). In the classroom\,&nbsp\;you'll&nbsp\;learn to use a combination of fabric layering and embroidery stitching to&nbsp\;render&nbsp\;your inspiration image in cloth.&nbsp\;You'll&nbsp\;leave with a uniquely personal memento of your time&nbsp\;here&nbsp\;ready to frame or use as a decorative patch or panel for a future project.\n\n\n\n\nView Full Textile Workshop Series\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nInstructor Bio\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nJudilee Fitzhugh is a textile artisan specializing in natural plant dyes and couture sewing. A tour of duty in Japan with the U.S. Navy sparked a lifelong affection for Japanese aesthetics\, indigo\, and plant fibers.\n\n\n\nShe earned her Certificate in Craft from the Oregon College of Art and Craft in 2002 and taught in the BFA and Studio School programs until the school’s closure in 2019. Her work combines natural materials\, vintage fabric remnants\, hand weaving\, and surface design to capture singular moments in history.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFeedback from Past Students\n\n\n\n\n“Fabulous location\, people\, and instruction. Judilee is so generous and positive.”\n\n\n\n\n\n“Loved these classes! The Garden + the people + the instructor + facility… all the stars lined up!”\n\n\n\n\n\n“Our teacher gave us the precious gift of artistic creativity and inspiration.”\n\n\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://wpmedia.japanesegarden.org/w:1853/h:1853/q:mauto/process:47393/id:e624b1099653d1a6275455233c161225/https://japanesegarden.org/landscapes.jpg
CATEGORIES:Classes &amp; Workshops
LOCATION:Yanai Classroom\, 611 SW Kingston Ave.\, Portland\, Oregon\, 97205\, United States
GEO:45.51862;-122.70843109999998
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=611 SW Kingston Ave.\, Portland\, Oregon\, 97205\, United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Yanai Classroom:geo:45.51862;-122.70843109999998
END:VEVENT
