 e are often called to come from a place of perpetual productivity\, botto
 mless capacity\, always giving and always "on". Yet the wholeness of who 
 we are requires periods of reflection\, receiving and renewal. When we do
  not honor this necessary balance\, the wisdom of our hearts is harder to
  hear.</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><em>What's growing in your life? 
 What needs to be nourished for further growth? What do you want to prune 
 or clear out?</em></p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><em>How do we listen 
 to and honor what we need to be whole and in balance amid the demands and
  desires of an abundant life\, in a way that allows for spaciousness\, au
 thenticity and joy?</em></p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><em>How do we t
 end to the garden of our lives and our work so that we can receive what w
 e need to flourish?</em></p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  Held during a
  time of peak growth and seasonal abundance\, this Courage to Lead® two-
 day workshop invites us into spacious time for reflection\, connection\, 
 and inner growth.</p><h4 style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Together we w
