 x-h="856" loading="lazy" data-optimized="true"/></picture> Krystal Marcin
 kiewicz\, MA\, LPC\, LMHC is a Licensed Professional Counselor and Clinic
 al Supervisor\, having earned her Masters Degree in Professional Mental H
 ealth Counseling from Lewis &amp\; Clark College in 2018. Drawing from an
  integrative feminist approach\, her work is grounded in person-centered 
 values\, emphasizing authentic connection\, and collaborative engagement.
  Her primary clinical focus is supporting clients in navigating identity 
 development\, body politics\, neurodivergence\, emotional codependency\, 
 highly sensitive personalities and other complex emotional experiences.</
 p><p style="line-height: 1.6\;">  In addition to clinical work\, Krystal 
 is also passionate in training and mentoring emerging counselors. She is 
 an adjunct professor\, teaching a wide variety of graduate counseling cou
 rses with an underlying emphasis on counselor identity development\, refl
 ective practice\, and cultivating professional resilience.</p><p style="l
 ine-height: 1.6\;">  In both the classroom\, and her clinical work\, Krys
 tal is committed to creating affirming spaces that honor intersectional i
 dentities and lived experience.</p><div id="lw_widget_470b39ba" class="lw
