 ntina Pishchanskaya-Cayanan\, LMFT\, CIMHP</strong>&#160\;is a Ukrainian 
 licensed marriage and family therapist with extensive experience in clini
 cal practice\, higher education\, and nonprofit leadership. She is the ow
 ner of Cayanan Counseling and Wellness\, a virtual private practice servi
 ng clients across Oregon and Washington. Her practice is dedicated to pro
 viding compassionate\, culturally attuned care with specializations in an
 xiety\, trauma\, and significant life adjustments. Valentina is EMDR-trai
 ned and integrates evidence-based\, trauma-informed approaches to help cl
 ients navigate change\, build resilience\, and foster lasting well-being.
 </p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  As a tenured faculty counselor at Cla
 rk College\, Valentina provides psychotherapy\, teaches\, and develops pr
 ograms to support diverse and underserved populations\, including Ukraini
 an students. She is also the Co-Founder and Vice President of DAWN Inc.\,
  where she leads humanitarian and medical aid initiatives in Ukraine and 
 supports refugee integration locally.</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  
 Valentina has presented at several conferences\, including the Northwest 
 Regional Equity Conference\, on the needs of Ukrainians and the importanc
 e of culturally responsive\, trauma-informed care. She has also spoken to
  policymakers\, healthcare providers\, and community leaders about the on
 going challenges faced by Ukrainians and ways to strengthen systems of su
 pport both locally and abroad.<br />  Through her clinical\, educational\
 , and nonprofit work\, Valentina is recognized for advancing resilience\,
  equity\, and culturally informed trauma care in both local and internati
 onal contexts.</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong><picture class="l
 w_image lw_image112607  lw_align_right"><source type="image/webp" srcset=
