 icture>Yulia Brockdorf\, RD\, LD\, CDCES\, CST\, NCC\, LPC\, BC-ADM\, BC-
 TMH\, LMHC\, FAIHM\, LN\, CD\, ACS\, FAWM</strong>&#160\;is a Ukrainian-A
 merican trauma psychotherapist and registered dietitian specializing in t
 reating complex trauma and culturally competent care. She is the develope
 r of the first combat psychotherapy model designed for delivery in active
  combat zones and has co-authored peer-reviewed publications on the psych
 ological impact of drone warfare. Ms. Brockdorf provides direct psychothe
 rapy to Ukrainian defenders along Ukraine's front lines and has trained m
 ental health professionals\, psychiatry residents\, and healthcare provid
 ers on trauma-informed approaches and working with Ukrainian populations.
 </p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  Ms. Brockdorf developed the trauma an
 d mental health course module <em>Connecting with Ukrainian Refugees: Mee
 ting Their Needs with Better Care and Key Service</em> for the Washington
  State Department of Health and has lectured at universities and medical 
 schools on culturally responsive care for displaced populations. Her work
  has been published in peer-reviewed literature and she has been featured
  on Oregon's Think Out Loud and other media outlets. She previously serve
 d as Board President of the Oregon Board of Licensed Dietitians.</p><p st
 yle="line-height: 1.5\;">  As president and co-founder of DAWN\, Inc.\, M
 s. Brockdorf has coordinated over $20 million in medical aid deliveries t
 o Ukraine. She serves on the executive team of DefenseTech for Ukraine an
 d advocates for U.S. support of Ukraine at state and federal levels\, inc
 luding meetings with NATO officials\, representatives of the European Par
 liament\, and members of the Government of Ukraine\, and champions both l
 ocal and international efforts in global security.</p><div id="lw_widget_
